<task>
As a GitHub assistant, create an implementation plan for the issue.
</task>

<context>
<issue>
Number: ${GH_CLAUDE_ISSUE_NUMBER}
Title: ${GH_ISSUE_TITLE}
URL: ${GH_ISSUE_URL}
Body: ${GH_ISSUE_BODY}
Labels: ${GH_ISSUE_LABELS}
</issue>

<comments>
${GH_ISSUE_COMMENTS}
</comments>
</context>

<focus>
${GH_ISSUE_FOCUS}
</focus>

<additional_context>
${GH_ISSUE_CONTEXT}
</additional_context>

<instructions>
Think step by step: first understand the issue requirements, then identify
the affected components, and finally break the work into concrete tasks.

If <focus> is empty, no specific focus area was requested — plan the full
implementation.
</instructions>

<rules>
- Focus on concrete engineering tasks rather than vague descriptions.
- Use sequential step IDs for implementation steps.
- If the issue lacks sufficient detail, highlight missing information.
- If <additional_context> is empty, no extra context was provided.
</rules>

<output_format>
First line: PR title — `# {title}`, under 72 chars
Include `Closes #${GH_CLAUDE_ISSUE_NUMBER}`
Implementation plan as TODO checklist
Format: GitHub-flavored Markdown
Output only the requested content.
Do not include preamble, commentary, or meta text.
Omit sections that are not relevant to the input.

<example>
# {title}

Closes #${GH_CLAUDE_ISSUE_NUMBER}

## Summary
{1–2 sentence description of the planned change}

## Implementation Plan
- [ ] T001 - {implementation step}
- [ ] T002 - {implementation step}
- [ ] T003 - {implementation step}

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] {criterion defining completion}
- [ ] {criterion defining completion}
</example>
</output_format>
